# Attributes that keep merges from parallel worktrees from breaking files
#
# `-merge` = git does not 3-way merge the file. On conflict, take one side and regenerate it.
# `-diff`  = treat as binary (keeps 1MB minified diffs out of logs and reviews).
#
# Why: of the files that needed conflict resolution in the last 60 merges, **tracked bundles came up 24 times**.
# git once 3-way merged a 1MB bundle and broke it; it had to be rebuilt from e2ee.ts.
# Generated files are meant to be regenerated, not merged.

# ---------- Generated files (regenerate on conflict; never merge) ----------
# Regenerate: bun run plugin:build (adapters/official/*/package.json)
*.bundle.js                                 -merge -diff
# Regenerate: bun scripts/catalog-build.ts (--check shows the diff against the committed file)
packages/core/registry/detectors.v1.json    -merge
# Regenerate: bash scripts/diagrams-build.sh (sources are docs/diagrams/*.md)
docs/diagrams.md                            -merge

# ---------- Lock files (take one side, then reinstall) ----------
bun.lock                                    -merge
broker/Cargo.lock                           -merge

# ---------- Binary (explicit by extension; don't rely on auto-detection) ----------
*.png                                       binary
*.gif                                       binary
*.jpg                                       binary
*.jpeg                                      binary
*.webp                                      binary
*.mp4                                       binary
*.ico                                       binary
*.woff                                      binary
*.woff2                                     binary

# ---------- Deliberately left out (with reasons) ----------
# No merge=union for docs/diagrams.md: union mixes both sides without conflict markers, which
#   silently breaks structured markdown. The fix for that file is one file per figure.
# No merge=mergiraf (a syntax-aware merge driver) yet: there is no bottle for this platform, so it
#   would be a source build, and attributes written before the driver is set in git config
#   **silently do nothing**. Add it in the same commit as the install.
